    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77283823_d24377ea",
        "filename": "oemlock/1.0/IOemLock.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1013030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-03T16:17:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What does \u0027vendor\u0027 mean here though - is it the OEM? Given that this affects carrier interests, wouldn\u0027t the carriers really want to be able to set this?\n\nThe way you write it now, it sounds like every OEM needs to modify system_server to implement a signing algorithm, but it\u0027s unclear over what data or using which key.",
      "parentUuid": "2ab532c1_40b86b7c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "c4aea5692571d35b83a2c5fc1dcc3b27d4634e9e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78dc1b11_a2429de0",
        "filename": "oemlock/1.0/IOemLock.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-03T16:35:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The flow would be something like this:\n\n- Carrier decides to allow OEM unlock\n- App on device sends proof of ID to server\n- Server signs a request to allow unlock of phone\n- App passes signature to HAL (system server just forwards the bytes and does nothing to it)\n- HAL implementation checks the signature\n\nSigning is on the server (i.e. not on the phone) and verification is in the HAL implementation. They must share a secret and both are controlled by the vendor.",
      "parentUuid": "77283823_d24377ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "c4aea5692571d35b83a2c5fc1dcc3b27d4634e9e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "312218ea_a611f78f",
        "filename": "oemlock/1.0/IOemLock.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1013030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-03T23:22:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, as long as the framework doesn\u0027t have to interpret it that is fine. I do wonder if it wouldn\u0027t be nicer to provide some guidance or even a requirement here on how to sign; as it is, the remote backend not only needs to know a shared secret, but it also needs to know how to compute the signature, which can be different on every Android device, depending on the HAL implementation they use.",
      "parentUuid": "78dc1b11_a2429de0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "c4aea5692571d35b83a2c5fc1dcc3b27d4634e9e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e55c28a2_e3bd9fd1",
        "filename": "oemlock/1.0/IOemLock.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-04T10:29:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The details of this are deliberately left to the carrier-vendor partnership. This is required if they are going to share a secret as that must be kept secret and not well documented. It is also fine to not have any crypto protection and so not requires a signature. The docs say the signature might not be needed but the non-Android parties involved will have to agree on what the process involved will be. Android itself is not involved in the business related aspect of this.",
      "parentUuid": "312218ea_a611f78f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "c4aea5692571d35b83a2c5fc1dcc3b27d4634e9e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
